CURRENT REQUIREMENTS BASELINE (latest choices supersede former stack/renderer requirements):
1 App-agnostic reusable Android MCP bridge; consuming agents own business workflows. No Lyft/Uber app logic or bridge business-monitoring/decision scheduler.
2 ALL available SDK/Binder/AIDL/protocol bindings mapped/versioned/exposed, not curated. Full inventory, generic invocation and explicit low-level options. Generated sources/provenance, unknown/unreachable/private/OEM evidence retained with reasons; no universal introspection or guessed wire contract.
3 MCP SERVER IS KOTLIN and UI ALSO KOTLIN, Jetpack Compose. This supersedes earlier Avalonia12/.NET management-stack requirement. One Android APK/UID/initial process; started foreground Kotlin service owns transport, policy, SQLite/catalog/runtime/resolution/backends/callbacks/groups; Compose Activity uses bounded unexported local service facade, cannot bypass owner authorization. Python extractors/offline references are tooling, not delivered Kotlin app.
4 SQLite client configuration, per-client permissions and configurable call logging. Declared permission metadata, actual Android/backend authority and MCP grants remain separate and canonical across generated/generic/raw paths.
5 Persistent UI-independent MCP service, optional boot, truthful AppBar/system running indicator with Android eligibility/notification limits; separate MCP readiness, device-view readiness and ADB health. No unconditional uptime guarantee.
6 Same-device paired ADB for uninstrumented apps and remote-host ADB loopback forwarding; on-demand screen.state/input.tap, agent decides timing/interpretation. No real phone actions in this task.
7 PORT AVALONIA.REMOTECONTROL INTERNALLY TO KOTLIN, RETAIN ARC PROTOCOL. Not merely external adapter. Separate controller Compose UI->SessionManager->ARCClient->Codec/model from target Listener->Router->AuthN/AuthZ->tree/action/input/frame/log adapters. Internal Kotlin ARC engine plus ComposeTargetAdapter and separate generic ADB backend. Retain compatible clients and exact pinned wire. External compatible targets may remain; no managed server/UI dependency.
8 Comprehensive Google public binding/permission catalog; immutable imports and source evidence, local overrides, schema versioning/future compatibility, CRUD/ETag/CAS/transitions and canonical binding policy. Namespace/package semantic physical re-sharding remains proposal, not requested implementation.
9 Startup device-resolved bindings AND types using observed platform major/minor, SDK extensions, OEM/build, installed modules and supported interface version/hash/reachability evidence. Full unavailable/unknown inventory, coherent type closure, atomic membership/variant selection and refresh on relevant backend/capability/catalog changes. No APIlevel-only guesses or authority inferred from existence.
10 Identify ALL callback roles/candidates: Binder interfaces, SDK listener/delegate/abstract classes, inherited methods, registration/cleanup pair/argument/token mapping and evidence/version classification; unknowns retained. Generic invocation accepts typed callback binding spec and returns finite registration result/subscription handle. Bounded event journal/stream identity/correlation/sequence/time/payload/errors, delivery/replay/dedup, buffering/overflow/oversize/backpressure, cancellation/death/revoke/disconnect/restart, authorization/logging. Synchronous return callback requires bounded LOCAL typed deadline/fallback/evidence or unsupported; cannot wait on remote agent/network. HIDL completion distinct from subscription.
